<title>JAPAN: TIFFE Euroyen futures fall on banks' swap payments.</title>
<headline>TIFFE Euroyen futures fall on banks' swap payments.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key December three-month Euroyen futures on TIFFE fell to 99.08 from the previous day's 99.14 on Wednesday, due to two and four-year interest rate swap payments by major Japanese banks, dealers said.</p>
<p>The payment was based on speculation that the Bank of Japan's &quot;tankan&quot; corporate survey due at 0200 GMT would confirm a healthy recovery of the Japanese economy, they said.</p>
